       "section": "action",
       "ids": [
        "clean:audit"
       ],
       "text": "Ten Support employees are flight risks and should be put on retention plans now. Reducing voluntary attrition would directly lower replacement costs and preserve institutional knowledge."
      },
      {
       "section": "action",
       "ids": [
        "seg:Department/Annual_Salary",
        "eda:Annual_Salary"
       ],
       "text": "Review the pay gap between Support ($62,996 average) and the organisation-wide median ($69,300) to assess whether compensation is competitive enough to retain staff in that department. Support is the lowest-paid department and may be contributing disproportionately to attrition."
      },
      {
       "section": "action",
       "ids": [
        "eda:Annual_Salary"
       ],
       "text": "Examine the high-salary outliers (up to $217,100) to confirm they are correctly classified and not data errors before using salary figures in any pay-equity or benchmarking work. Outliers inflate the mean and could distort department-level comparisons."
